# web-hooks

> **Purpose:** Keep hooks clean, single-purpose and leak-free.
>
> **Applies to:** `apps/web/src/hooks/**`

## Shape
- One hook per file, named `useX.ts`.
- Each hook does one job. If it does two, split it.
- Return a typed object (`{ data, error, isLoading }`), not a long tuple.
- No JSX and no styling inside hooks.

## Data
- Data hooks call only the services in `src/services/`.
- Validate data with `@stamp/schema` before returning it.

## Effects
- Clean up every effect: close `EventSource`, clear timers, abort `AbortController`.
- Keep dependency arrays complete. Never disable `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps`.
- Never call hooks conditionally or in loops.

## State
- Derive values instead of storing duplicate state.
- Use `useMemo` and `useCallback` only for a real, measured cost.

## Reuse
- When a component has more than one effect or tangled state, move that logic into a hook.
- Extract pure logic from hooks into `src/utils/` and test it there.
- Reuse one shared async-state helper instead of rewriting loading and error logic in every hook.
